<title>GERMANY: Germans seek to export free mkt wheat, barley, rye.</title>
<headline>Germans seek to export free mkt wheat, barley, rye.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids to export 26,000 tonnes of free market wheat with restitutions in a range between 18.74 and 21.75 Ecus a tonne, state grain intervention board BLE said.</p>
<p>Under a weekly EU export tender, BLE also received bids for 1,000 tonnes of free market barley, where a rebate of 31.49 Ecus/t was sought, and for 2,000 tonnes of free market rye with subsidies in a 31.99-35.95 Ecus/t range.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
